## Claude — 2026-09-22 15:50 (pycache, live test result)

🙏 **pycache: my fault.** My Python test runs left `__pycache__` in the Prompt-queue root, and Edge won't load an extension that has a "_" name there. It is gitignored, so I never saw it.
✅ Fixed permanently (`d0d54a5`): a root `conftest.py` stops Python writing caches and deletes them after every pytest run, and a jest test fails if any "_" name is in the root (checked: fails on a planted `__pycache__`, passes after the cleanup). The rule is also in memory.
✅ Your reload worked at 15:23:50.
🔴 **Live job 1 failed with `composer_not_ready`.** The new error codes made that visible at once. The root cause is verified live:
- bridge job tabs open in the background (hidden);
- ChatGPT's lazy new-chat page mounts its real composer only when the tab renders a frame, and hidden tabs render none;
- one forced frame (a debugger screenshot) mounted it instantly, with the text carried over.
⏳ Fix S8.3b is with codex terra. For a few seconds, only on hidden new-chat job tabs, the extension forces frames through `chrome.debugger` until the composer mounts, then detaches.
- ⚠️ This adds the `debugger` permission to Prompt Queue. Edge shows a "started debugging this browser" bar for about 1–2 s per new-chat job.
- The alternative is switching to the job tab, which would steal your focus. Say so if you'd prefer that.

